.TH GIT-WORKFLOW-COMMIT 1 2026-10-03 git-workflow "git-workflow manual"
.SH NAME
git-workflow-commit \- commit with the message as plain words
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git workflow commit
.RB [ \-\-amend ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.RI [ message ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Commit the staged changes. Every word is part of the message, so
.B git workflow commit fix the bug
commits "fix the bug". With no message, asks for one.
If nothing is staged, shows the status and offers to stage everything
.RB ( "git add \-A" ).
.PP
Committing on a protected branch warns first, or stops when
.B workflow.strict
is true.
.PP
Arguments starting with "\-" are refused, because they are almost always
.BR git\-commit (1)
flags typed from habit
.RB ( "git workflow commit \-m fix"
would otherwise commit "\-m fix"). Put
.B \-\-
before a message that really starts with a dash.
.PP
The shell still reads the words before git does: quote a message that
contains
.BR # ,
.BR ' ,
.BR * ,
.B ?
or
.BR ! .
.PP
With the default aliases
.RB ( "git workflow aliases install" )
this is also
.BR "git c" ;
the 1.x name
.B c
works after
.B git workflow
too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-amend
Amend the last commit
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-workflow\-quick\-commit (1),
.BR git\-workflow (1)
